notes['Loser']=('FAQ p16', 'Loser Wild is played before encounter cards are selected.')
notes['Oracle']=('Rulebook p14; FAQ p18; FAQ p6', 'Against Sorcerer, foresee first: Sorcerer plays faceup, then Oracle chooses facedown; after both are selected Sorcerer can switch them. Against Gambler, Gambler must reveal or bluff before Oracle chooses. In the official Oracle Wild example, play the flare faceup in front of you outside the hands, mix the hands together, take your new hand at random from the mixed cards, then return the flare to hand when its effect finishes.')
notes['Filch']=('FAQ pp12–13; original rulebook p5', "After Sorcerer switches cards, take the card ending before your opponent. Clone keeping has precedence; Filch versus Fido uses ordinary timing. You cannot take Gambler's unchallenged facedown card because it goes beneath the deck rather than to discard. The classic Filch flare is revealed only when its cheating user is caught; it may then be zapped. Its printed Wild, as any player in any phase, permits illicit warp retrieval to colonies or taking deck/discard cards; being caught costs one ship to warp and returns the items caught being filched. Once revealed, deck and discards are placed next to that player. Use only one Filch flare version. The classic Filch Super, as any player during Reveal, permits filching any other player's used encounter card whether you participated in that encounter or not.")

# Source-backed Gambler positive-holdings precision, corrections07.
notes['Gambler']=('FAQ pp3,14; FAQ p5', 'Against Oracle you must reveal or announce your bluff before Oracle chooses a card. On Gambler Super, the old term token means ship. The standard printed Sorcerer incompatibility is retained here; the FAQ permits relaxing it if players accept that Sorcerer may know the card. The losing player chooses extra penalty ships under their control outside the encounter, ordinarily ships on their colonies in this original-base scope.')

# Source-described Fido flare acquisition, corrections08.
notes['Fido']=('FAQ p13; FAQ p4', 'Take only an actual encounter card played as such, not an encounter card merely discarded by Plague, Fodder or Reserve. Clone keeps before discarding; Fido competes with Filch using ordinary timing. For the Fido flare effect described by the FAQ, the forced discard-pile draw takes its top card.')

